{"id": "EUVD-2026-99016", "enisaUuid": "10cb50ff-de72-36a3-8373-fe2059b674bb", "description": "Fossify File Manager through 1.6.2 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows crafted ZIP archives to write files outside the extraction folder by bypassing an unanchored startsWith check. Attackers can supply archive entries like ../<name>_x/file to create or overwrite files in sibling folders when a user extracts the archive.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T18:50:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-17T00:38:03", "baseScore": 4.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:A/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/Hk2woGjsze", "https://github.com/FossifyOrg/File-Manager/blob/82b3c98c9a7b90d8af2c2ff0c39c87f5917e1b08/app/src/main/kotlin/org/fossify/filemanager/activities/DecompressActivity.kt#L161-L189", "https://github.com/FossifyOrg/File-Manager/releases/tag/1.6.2", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/fossify-file-manager-through-1.6.2-zip-slip-path-traversal-via-decompressactivity"], "aliases": ["GHSA-3q2q-qm6m-5wjv", "CVE-2026-110232"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e4ed8fdc-faf6-36d4-9fce-25cbee19837a", "product": {"name": "Fossify File Manager", "vendor": {"name": "Fossify"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.6.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7dfc9708-50af-3bd3-a3d0-c3938d720c77", "vendor": {"name": "Fossify"}}], "isExploited": false}